Here is a complete, step-by-step guide to building a full-stack web application using **React** (Frontend) and **Node.js/Express** (Backend).

We will build a simple **"Task Manager"** app where you can add tasks and view them.

### Prerequisites
*   Node.js installed.
*   A code editor (VS Code recommended).

---

### Part 1: Project Structure
Create a folder named `my-app` and set up two subfolders: `client` (React) and `server` (Node).

```text
my-app/
├── client/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── App.js
│   │   └── index.js
│   └── package.json
└── server/
    ├── index.js
    └── package.json
```

---

### Part 2: The Backend (Node & Express)

1.  Open your terminal in the `server` folder.
2.  Initialize the project and install dependencies:
    ```bash
    npm init -y
    npm install express cors body-parser
    ```

3.  Create a file named `index.js` inside the `server` folder and paste this code:

```javascript
// server/index.js
const express = require('express');
const cors = require('cors');
const bodyParser = require('body-parser');

const app = express();
const PORT = 5000;

// Middleware
app.use(cors()); // Allow React to talk to Node
app.use(bodyParser.json());

// In-memory Database (Dummy Data)
let tasks = [
    { id: 1, text: "Buy groceries", completed: false },
    { id: 2, text: "Learn React", completed: true }
];

// API: Get all tasks
app.get('/api/tasks', (req, res) => {
    res.json(tasks);
});

// API: Add a new task
app.post('/api/tasks', (req, res) => {
    const { text } = req.body;
    if (!text) {
        return res.status(400).json({ error: "Text is required" });
    }

    const newTask = {
        id: tasks.length + 1,
        text: text,
        completed: false
    };

    tasks.push(newTask);
    res.json(newTask);
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
    console.log(`Server running on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
});
```

4.  Update `server/package.json` to add a start script:
    ```json
    "scripts": {
      "start": "node index.js",
      "dev": "nodemon index.js"
    }
    ```
    *(Note: If you don't have nodemon, install it with `npm install -g nodemon`)*.

